/-!
# Whole-space strong convergence controls every nonlinear Fourier row

The infinite fixed-output convolution is locally Lipschitz on the whole
transverse `ℓ²` Fourier carrier.  Time Cauchy--Schwarz therefore gives the
genuine bilinear mapping law

```text
L²_t(ℓ²) × L²_t(ℓ²) → L¹_t(ℂ³)
```

for every fixed output frequency.  This module applies that law to the
actual common-time trajectories generated by arbitrary critical scale
paths and rewrites the three time integrals as the exact norms of their
whole space-time `L²` representatives.

No pointwise energy ceiling, Fourier cutoff, support union, maximum shell,
path length, target limit, or continuation witness enters the theorem
mouth.
-/

